    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Deccan empire founded in 753 by Dantidurga, who overthrew his Chalukya overlords; its capital from Amoghavarsha I was Manyakheta.</li><li>Its armies reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> and Kanchi, and Arab writers counted its king, the Balhara, among the world’s four great kings.</li><li>It carved the Kailasa temple at Ellora and fostered the earliest surviving Kannada literature and major Jain scholarship.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The last Rashtrakuta claimant, Indra IV, ended his life in 982 by sallekhana, the Jain ritual fast to death, at the hilltop shrine of Shravanabelagola.</p></aside>
    </section>

